From f3968f6d447cb4f827eecac86c330d991c513a00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:44:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 44/45] Copy a heap texture into a buffer from its resident

A texture-to-buffer copy resolved its source to guest bytes. A heap
texture has none: what a pass rendered into it lives in the engine's
resident. It shares the view's object tag, so the copy decoded it as a
view, failed (blit_fail reason=view_desc_decode) and left the buffer as
it was. A probe in the guest cleared a heap texture and copied it out in
six formats and read zeros every time, where a private texture, a shared
one and a linear one each read back the clear colour.

The copy now reads the heap texture's resident back and writes the rows
in the texture's own format, through RGBA8 as the guest-page store's
copying arm does. A heap texture no pass has rendered into is refused by
name (t2b_heap_unrendered); a clear with no draw does not establish the
resident yet, which is what the probe's copy now reports.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../reims-vgpu/src/runtime/blit_exec/mod.rs   | 151 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 151 insertions(+)

